---
// api-docs-read: static About page — no external API/protocol surface, only a booking link, mailto and LinkedIn.
// About (site architecture doc, trust pages, 26 Nov 2026). The only page that names the founder (Russell's rule,
// 26 Nov 2026). Holds #engagements (prices the AI-work pages cite) and #method (how pages are sourced and checked).
// The record below is the founder's own account, moved from the archived offer page; it is labeled as such.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ConsultingCta from '../components/ConsultingCta.astro';

const sources = [
  { n: 1, name: 'US Census Bureau, The Microstructure of AI Diffusion, working paper CES-WP-26-25 (April 2026)', url: 'https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2026/adrm/CES-WP-26-25.html', what: '66% of firms that use AI use it only to help with tasks; AI-related job cuts happened at 2% of firms.' },
  { n: 2, name: 'Zavient FinExtractBench (November 2026)', url: '/ai-work/ai-document-processing.html#own-data', what: 'Our benchmark of 30 private fund reports, 781 pages, with every answer written by hand and locked before any tool ran.' },
];
const fn = (n) => `#fn-${n}`;
const updated = '27 November 2026';
---
<Base title="About Zavient: who we are and how we work" description="Who runs Zavient, how an engagement works and what it costs, and how we source and check every number on this site." canonical="https://zavient.com/about.html" updated="2026-11-27">
  <header class="article-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="label">About</div>
    <h1>About Zavient: who we are and <span class="hl">how we work</span></h1>
    <span class="bluf-label">Bottom line</span>
    <div class="bluf">
      <ul>
        <li>Zavient helps companies of 40 to 500 people put AI to work in any function and any industry.</li>
        <li>The goal is AI that helps your people do more, not AI that replaces them.</li>
        <li>Work starts with a free 30-minute diagnostic. Paid work is a fixed-scope sprint, then optional advisory.</li>
        <li>Every market number on this site links to its source. Our own benchmarks show their method and limits.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <nav class="on-page" aria-label="On this page"><div class="label" style="margin-top:18px;">On this page</div><ol>
      <li><a href="#why">Why Zavient exists</a></li>
      <li><a href="#founder">Who runs it</a></li>
      <li><a href="#engagements">How we work</a></li>
      <li><a href="#method">How we check our numbers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#limits">What we won't do</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">How to reach us</a></li>
    </ol></nav>
  </div></header>

  <article class="article-body"><div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="why">Why Zavient exists</h2>
    <p>Mid-size companies hear a lot about AI and get little help choosing where to start. We are a small firm, and we sell no software.</p>
    <p>We sit in between. We tell you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which workflow to start with, in any part of the business.</li>
      <li>Whether to buy or build, and what to test before you spend.</li>
      <li>How AI can take the reading, matching and first drafts, so your team keeps the judgment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Most firms already use AI this way. 66% of firms that use AI use it only to help with tasks<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(1)} aria-label="Source 1">1</a></sup>.</p>

    <h2 id="founder">Who runs it</h2>
    <div class="founder-card">
      <img src="/russell-miller.jpg" alt="Russell Miller, founder of Zavient" width="128" height="128" loading="lazy" />
      <p><strong>Russell Miller, founder.</strong> About 20 years across B2B software, AI and machine learning, and private equity. Mathematics degree from MIT and an MBA from Texas A&amp;M (<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/russellmiller" rel="me">Russell on LinkedIn</a>).</p>
    </div>
    <p>His record, in his own account (client names withheld). Unlike the rest of the site, these numbers are not footnoted:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Machine learning in production:</strong> built an ML bidding system for search ads. Credited with over $20M revenue and over $8M EBITDA (profit before interest, taxes and write-downs).</li>
      <li><strong>AI for a B2B marketplace:</strong> AI that rewrote headlines in real time. 18% more click-throughs and over $900K in new pipeline.</li>
      <li><strong>Ad testing at an automotive marketplace:</strong> 5 times the click-through rate at 40% lower cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Operating role:</strong> COO of a private-equity-backed software company through its turnaround and sale.</li>
      <li><strong>Deals:</strong> five years as an independent sponsor (raising money deal by deal) alongside CIVC, Stonehenge and BlackRock, on deals from $7M to over $300M.</li>
      <li><strong>Benchmarks:</strong> built FinExtractBench, our test of AI tools on financial documents<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(2)} aria-label="Source 2">2</a></sup>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You work with Russell directly, not a team of juniors.</p>

    <h2 id="engagements">How we work</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Free 30-minute diagnostic.</strong> Bring one workflow and what it costs you today. You leave knowing buy or build, what to test, the rules and rough cost, with no obligation.</li>
      <li><strong>30-day AI Sprint, fixed scope.</strong> You get:
        <ul>
          <li>The 2 or 3 AI bets that pay back first, ranked by payoff and effort.</li>
          <li>Specs your team or a vendor can build from.</li>
          <li>A written case for your board, lender or partners.</li>
          <li>A 90-day plan with owners, and what not to do.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Ongoing advisory, if you want it.</strong> Two working sessions a month, plus questions answered between them, while the work ships. Quarterly commitment, renewed only if both sides want to.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Building the software itself is quoted per job, or done by your team or a vendor from our specs. You own the specs, the code and the results.</p>

    <h2 id="method">How we check our numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Every market claim has a source.</strong> Each number links to a numbered source at the foot of the page, with two or more sources where they exist.</li>
      <li><strong>Our own tests show their method.</strong> In FinExtractBench, our test of AI on financial documents, we wrote the right answers first, before any tool ran<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(2)} aria-label="Source 2">2</a></sup>. Each page lists the sample, what was measured and the limits.</li>
      <li><strong>We say what the numbers don't prove.</strong> A test on 30 documents is not a test on your documents, so we tell you to re-run it on your own files.</li>
      <li><strong>We use AI to help research and draft.</strong> Every number still links to the place it came from, so you can check it yourself.</li>
      <li><strong>Corrections.</strong> If you find an error, email <a href="mailto:hello@zavient.com">hello@zavient.com</a>. We fix it and update the page's date.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="limits">What we won't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Plan AI whose main goal is cutting your staff.</li>
      <li>Recommend tools your team can't check.</li>
      <li>Lock you in. You keep the specs and can build with anyone.</li>
      <li>Hand you a 200-page slide deck.</li>
      <li>Run AI experiments with no measure of what they're worth. If we can't find the return, we'll tell you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="contact">How to reach us</h2>
    <p>Book the <a href="https://calendar.app.google/2xXiMLiamRFtfFKH9">free 30-minute diagnostic</a>, or email <a href="mailto:hello@zavient.com">hello@zavient.com</a> with two sentences on the work. A person reads every email.</p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <ol class="sources">
      {sources.map((s) => <li id={`fn-${s.n}`}><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a>. {s.what}</li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="byline">By Zavient &middot; last reviewed {updated}</p>
  </div></article>

  <ConsultingCta job="AI in any part of your business" heading="Start with a free 30-minute diagnostic" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Zavient',
    legalName: 'Zavient LLC',
    url: 'https://zavient.com/',
    logo: 'https://zavient.com/favicon.svg',
    description: 'AI consulting for companies of 40 to 500 people, across every kind of work and every industry.',
    founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Russell Miller', jobTitle: 'Founder', sameAs: ['https://www.linkedin.com/in/russellmiller'] },
    contactPoint: { '@type': 'ContactPoint', contactType: 'sales', email: 'hello@zavient.com' },
  })} />
</Base>
